. **************************************************************************
. * H3: Income pooling & WorkShare – Improved DiD Analysis             *
. * Authors: [REDACTED], [REDACTED]      
. 
. /********************************************************************
> * CHANGE LOG (July 2025):
> * Based on feedback, we revised the H3 
> * analysis to produce a single result per hypothesis. Specifically:
> *
> * - We dropped the "Joint financial decision" outcome and the 
> *   "AbsDev_Work" and "AbsDev_Total" time-use measures.
> * - We retained only "AbsDev_Home" (deviation from equal housework 
> *   distribution) as the outcome for H3.
> *
> * This ensures one consistent DiD result aligned with our pre-analysis 
> * plan (see Table 1 and Section 6).
> * This variable captures the extent to which partners share 
> * responsibility for essential, recurring household tasks that directly 
> * support family functioning (e.g., cleaning, cooking, laundry). 
> * Among the available time-use outcomes, housework most directly reflects 
> * negotiated task division and shared labor within the home.
> *
> * We view this as the most conceptually grounded behavioral measure for 
> * testing H3: whether having daughters leads to greater gender equality 
> * in the household. 
> ********************************************************************/        
>                        *
. **************************************************************************
. * clear all
. 
. version 18

. set maxvar 10000


. 
. *----------------------------------------------------------------------------
. * INSTALL PACKAGES * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. *----------------------------------------------------------------------------
. ssc install mdesc
checking mdesc consistency and verifying not already installed...
all files already exist and are up to date.

. 
. *-----------------------------
. * CONFIGURE FILE PATHS  (Please do not change)
. /*
> * the following code automatically sets paths based on where you saved the di
> stributed file-package on your system *
> *-----------------------------
> 
> if strpos("`c(pwd)'", "code") {
> global ROOT "`c(pwd)'/.."
> }
> else {
> global ROOT "`c(pwd)'"
> }
> global IN "$ROOT/data/raw" // folder, in which the original datasets are stor
> ed
> global DATA "$ROOT/data/derived" // folder for datasets
> global OUT "$ROOT/out" // folder for output (results, tables)
> 
> */
. 
. *============================================================================
> ===
. **# Data Preparation * 
. *============================================================================
> ===
. 
. *----------------------------------------------------------------------------
. * LOAD AND MERGE DATA * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. *----------------------------------------------------------------------------
. 
. use "$IN/ppathl.dta", clear // use ppathl as a starting dataset
(SOEP-Core, v37 (EU Edition), doi:10.5684/soep.core.v37eu)

. 
. * Merge ppathl with all datasets, that you deem relevant for your analysis. (
> Tip: use keepusing() to specify which variables to keep from the using datase
> t; the default is all.)
. 
. * biobirth contains information on fertility history
. merge m:1 pid using "$IN/biobirth.dta", nogen keep(master matches)
(variable pid was long, now double to accommodate using data's values)
(variable cid was long, now double to accommodate using data's values)
(variable gebjahr was int, now double to accommodate using data's values)
(label sex already defined)
(label sex_EN already defined)

    Result                      Number of obs
    -----------------------------------------
    Not matched                             0
    Matched                           663,123  
    -----------------------------------------

. * pgen contains user-friendly data on the individual level that are consolida
> ted from different sources
. merge 1:1 pid syear using "$IN/pgen.dta", nogen keep(master matches)
(variable syear was long, now double to accommodate using data's values)

    Result                      Number of obs
    -----------------------------------------
    Not matched                             0
    Matched                           663,123  
    -----------------------------------------

. * pl contains all variables from the individual questionnaire
. merge 1:1 pid syear using "$IN/pl.dta", nogen keep(master matches)
(variable inputdataset was str6, now str9 to accommodate using data's values)
(label cid_EN already defined)
(label pid_EN already defined)
(label cid already defined)

    Result                      Number of obs
    -----------------------------------------
    Not matched                             0
    Matched                           663,123  
    -----------------------------------------

. * hgen contains generated variables on household level from the household int
> erview; use for household net income
. merge m:1 hid syear using "$IN/hgen.dta", nogen keep(master matches) keepusin
> g(hid syear hghinc)
(label iyear already defined)
(label iyear_EN already defined)

    Result                      Number of obs
    -----------------------------------------
    Not matched                             0
    Matched                           663,123  
    -----------------------------------------

. 
. label language EN // change language of the labels to English

. 
. ************************************
. save "$DATA/h3_dataset.dta", replace // save merged dataset
file C:\Users\dalbrecht\Research
    Projects\ManyDaughters\ManyDaughters_DataPreprocessing/data/derived_confi
    > dential/95%-sample/h3_dataset.dta saved

. ************************************
. 
. *----------------------------------------------------------------------------
. * PREPARE VARIABLES * 
. *----------------------------------------------------------------------------
. use "$DATA/h3_dataset.dta", clear

. 
. *============================
. * Construct outcomes                                          *
. *============================
. 
. * 3.1 Joint financial decision making
. gen byte JointDecision = (plc0011 == 3)

. label variable JointDecision "Joint financial decision equal say"

. 
. *============================
. * Construct DiD regressors                                     *
. *============================
. * identify first‐child sex and timing
. bysort pid: egen byte Daughter = max(kidsex01==2)

. bysort pid: egen byte Son      = max(kidsex01==1)

. bysort pid (syear): assert Daughter==Daughter[1]

. 
. gen int   yearFirstChild = kidgeb01

. gen byte Post            = (syear >= kidgeb01) if Daughter==1 | Son==1
(216,893 missing values generated)

. gen byte Man             = (sex==1)

. 
. *============================
. *  Controls (PaP Table 4)                                               *
. *============================
. mdesc sumkids pgfamstd plh0258_h sampreg bioage migback pgbilzeit hghinc pgem
> plst pgexpft

    Variable    |     Missing          Total     Percent Missing
----------------+-----------------------------------------------
        sumkids |           0        663,123           0.00
       pgfamstd |     143,310        663,123          21.61
      plh0258_h |     148,633        663,123          22.41
        sampreg |           0        663,123           0.00
         bioage |           0        663,123           0.00
        migback |           0        663,123           0.00
      pgbilzeit |     143,310        663,123          21.61
         hghinc |      80,120        663,123          12.08
       pgemplst |     143,310        663,123          21.61
        pgexpft |     143,310        663,123          21.61
----------------+-----------------------------------------------

. 
. * number of children (pool 5+)
. gen nchild = sumkids

. replace nchild = 5 if nchild > 5
(7,063 real changes made)

. 
. * marital status
. gen mastat = pgfamstd == 1 | pgfamstd == 6 | pgfamstd == 7 | pgfamstd == 8

. replace mastat = . if pgfamstd == .
(143,310 real changes made, 143,310 to missing)

. label define mastat 0 "Unmarried" 1 "Married"

. label values mastat mastat

. 
. * region of residence/origin
. replace sampreg        = sampreg - 1
(663,123 real changes made)

. replace birthregion_ew = birthregion_ew - 1
(663,123 real changes made)

. label define ew 0 "West" 1 "East"

. label values sampreg ew

. label values birthregion_ew ew

. 
. * age & squared
. sort pid piyear

. gen age    = syear - gebjahr

. gen age_sq = age^2

. 
. * work experience & squared
. gen exp    = pgexpft
(143,310 missing values generated)

. gen exp_sq = exp^2
(143,310 missing values generated)

. 
. * employment indicator
. gen byte emplyd = inlist(pgemplst,1,2)

. label define emp 0 "Not employed" 1 "Employed"

. label values emplyd emp

. 
. label variable hghinc "Household net income"

. 
. * controls list (PaP Table 4)
. local controls2 "i.nchild i.mastat i.sampreg age age_sq exp exp_sq i.migback 
> pgbilzeit hghinc i.emplyd"

. global controls "`controls2'"

. 
. *============================
. *  Sample restrictions (PaP §4)                                         *
. *============================
. keep if inlist(pop,1,2) // only keeping participants from private households 
> and with complete information 
(89,279 observations deleted)

. * plausible ages & valid region
. keep if sampreg>=0 & inrange(age,18,50)
(262,973 observations deleted)

. * must have become first‐time parent
. keep if yearFirstChild>0
(103,248 observations deleted)

. 
. *============================
. *  Compute Time‐Use shares                                      *
. *============================
. * restrict to wives & couples
. keep if parid>0
(32,698 observations deleted)

. 
. * merge partner time‐use data
. tempfile partner

. preserve

.     keep pid syear pli0012_h pli0016_h pli0043_h pli0007_h pli0003_h pli0038_
> h

.     rename pid parid

.     rename pli0012_h HomeSat_p

.     rename pli0016_h HomeSun_p

.     rename pli0043_h HomeWkday_p

.    
.     save `partner', replace
(file C:\Users\DALBRE~1\AppData\Local\Temp\ST_1eec_000002.tmp not found)
file C:\Users\DALBRE~1\AppData\Local\Temp\ST_1eec_000002.tmp saved as .dta
    format

. restore

. merge 1:1 parid syear using "`partner'", nogenerate keep(match)
(variable parid was long, now double to accommodate using data's values)
(label pli0003_h already defined)
(label pli0007_h already defined)
(label pli0012_h already defined)
(label pli0016_h already defined)
(label pli0038_h already defined)
(label pli0043_h already defined)
(label syear_EN already defined)
(label pli0003_h_EN already defined)
(label pli0007_h_EN already defined)
(label pli0012_h_EN already defined)
(label pli0016_h_EN already defined)
(label pli0038_h_EN already defined)
(label pli0043_h_EN already defined)
(label pid_EN already defined)

    Result                      Number of obs
    -----------------------------------------
    Not matched                             0
    Matched                           148,346  
    -----------------------------------------

. 
. * recode negatives to missing
. foreach v in pli0012_h pli0016_h pli0043_h  {
  2.     replace `v' = . if `v' < 0
  3. }
(77,502 real changes made, 77,502 to missing)
(77,872 real changes made, 77,872 to missing)
(6,936 real changes made, 6,936 to missing)

. foreach v in HomeSat_p HomeSun_p HomeWkday_p {
  2.     replace `v' = . if `v' < 0
  3. }
(77,502 real changes made, 77,502 to missing)
(77,872 real changes made, 77,872 to missing)
(6,936 real changes made, 6,936 to missing)

. 
. * compute weekly totals
. gen HomeWeek_r  = pli0012_h + pli0016_h + 5*pli0043_h
(85,031 missing values generated)

. gen HomeWeek_p  = HomeSat_p + HomeSun_p + 5*HomeWkday_p
(85,031 missing values generated)

. 
. * keep only complete couples
. keep if !missing(HomeWeek_r, HomeWeek_p) 
(88,638 observations deleted)

. 
. * allocate to spouses
. gen wife_HomeWeek    = cond(sex==2, HomeWeek_r, HomeWeek_p)

. gen husband_HomeWeek = cond(sex==1, HomeWeek_r, HomeWeek_p)

. 
. * compute wife shares
. gen HomeShare  = wife_HomeWeek / (wife_HomeWeek + husband_HomeWeek)
(26 missing values generated)

. 
. * deviations from equality
. gen AbsDev_Home  = abs(HomeShare - 0.5)
(26 missing values generated)

. label variable AbsDev_Home "Absolute deviation from equal distribution of hou
> sework"

. 
. * * Flags for AbsDev_Home availability pre/post
. bysort pid: egen byte has_AbsDev_Home_pre = max(!missing(`y') & !Post)

. bysort pid: egen byte has_AbsDev_Home_post = max(!missing(`y') & Post)

. 
. 
. 
. *============================
. *  DiD regression: TotalShare       
. *Regression : y_i,t = β_0 + β_1*Daughter_i + β_2*Post_i,t + β_3*Daughter_i × 
> Post_i,t + \gamma*X_i,t + \varepsilon_i,t
. * The study employs a difference-in-differences (DiD) design to test whether 
> having daughters leads to moreEqual Share of Hours. The approach leverages th
> e quasi-random assignment of child sex to compare individuals whose first chi
> ld is a girl (treatment group) versus those whose first child is a boy (contr
> ol group), examining changes in Hours Division before and after childbirth.  
>                               
. *============================
. 
. keep if has_AbsDev_Home_pre & has_AbsDev_Home_post & Man == 0
(56,363 observations deleted)

. xtset pid syear

Panel variable: pid (unbalanced)
 Time variable: syear, 2001 to 2019, but with gaps
         Delta: 1 unit

. xtreg AbsDev_Home i.Daughter##i.Post $controls, vce(cluster cid)

